.TH CHTTPSVR_SET_ENGINE_LOGGER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_set_engine_logger \- set the logger for engine-level diagnostics
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_set_engine_logger(clog cl);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Derives a child logger from cl, adds the field
component=http-server-engine to it, and installs it as the diagnostics
logger of the shared reactor.  It closes the logger derived by an
earlier call and, when there is one, the fallback logger of a running
engine.

The reactor logs to this handle at exactly three points: a TLS
handshake failure, a listen-socket bind failure, and each pass of the
idle-timeout sweep that closes one or more connections.  When no
logger from this function is in place as the engine starts, the engine
installs a fallback logger automatically, which writes to fd 2 at
level CLOG_FATAL, like the internal stderr-only, FATAL-only logger of
ccol_create_chttpsvr.  All three diagnostic points above log below
CLOG_FATAL, so the min_level of that fallback logger filters every one
of them out, and the fallback logger is silent in practice.  Use this
function to install a more informative logger.

You can call this function at any time: before the first
chttpsvr_start, while the reactor is already running, and after a
full engine stop.  The child logger serves the currently running
reactor, if there is one, and every reactor that a later
chttpsvr_start brings up after a full engine stop, until another call
of this function replaces it.

cl must not be CLOG_INVALID.  The library owns the derived child
logger and closes it when another call replaces it, or at process
exit or library unload when no engine is running at that point; the
caller must not close it.  The caller keeps ownership of cl and may
close cl at any time, because the child logger is a handle of its own
and keeps the destination of cl open for as long as it lives.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args when cl is CLOG_INVALID.
ccol_not_enough_memory when the child logger cannot be
                  allocated.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_start (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_wait (3)
